		'image-prompt-styleguide',
		'Image Prompting Style Guide: Midjourney, DALL·E, Imagen and Stable Diffusion',
		'Prompting',
		'Intermediate',
		true,
		'The structure of a great image prompt, lighting and lens words, style references, negative prompts and tool-specific parameters.',
		'<h3>The image prompt formula</h3><p><strong>Subject + action + setting + composition + lighting + style + details + parameters.</strong></p><pre>A young Indian software engineer coding at night in a small Bengaluru apartment,\nover-the-shoulder shot, warm desk lamp and blue monitor glow, cinematic,\nshallow depth of field, 35mm lens, rain on the window, highly detailed</pre><h3>Words that change everything</h3><ul><li><strong>Shot</strong>: close-up, wide shot, top-down flat lay, isometric, macro.</li><li><strong>Lens</strong>: 24mm (wide), 50mm (natural), 85mm (portrait), tilt-shift (miniature look).</li><li><strong>Light</strong>: golden hour, soft studio light, rim light, neon, overcast, volumetric fog.</li><li><strong>Style</strong>: photorealistic, 3D render, claymation, flat vector, watercolour, line art, low poly.</li><li><strong>Mood</strong>: calm, dramatic, playful, futuristic, minimal.</li></ul><h3>Tool notes</h3><ul><li><strong>Midjourney</strong>: parameters at the end: <code>--ar 16:9</code> aspect ratio, <code>--stylize</code> how artistic, <code>--chaos</code> variety, <code>--no</code> things to avoid, <code>--seed</code> repeatability. Use image references for consistent style.</li><li><strong>ChatGPT / DALL·E and Gemini / Imagen</strong>: write in full sentences; ask for edits in plain words (“make the background white, keep the person”). Good with text inside images.</li><li><strong>Stable Diffusion</strong>: use a negative prompt (blurry, extra fingers, watermark, low quality), set steps (25–40) and CFG (5–8), choose a model that matches the style.</li></ul><h3>For thumbnails and ads</h3><ul><li>One subject, big and clear, high contrast, space for text.</li><li>Generate the image without text, then add text in Canva or Figma for sharp results.</li></ul><h3>Rules to respect</h3><ul><li>No real people’s faces without permission, no copied logos or characters.</li><li>Check each tool’s licence before commercial use.</li></ul>'
