		'From Python basics to a deployed AI project and a job-ready portfolio, with weekly goals, projects and interview prep.',
		'<h3>Weeks 1–3: foundations</h3><ul><li>Python: functions, lists/dicts, files, virtual environments, Git.</li><li>Data: NumPy, pandas, charts. Do 3 small analyses on public datasets.</li><li>Maths you actually need: averages, probability basics, vectors and dot products.</li></ul><h3>Weeks 4–6: machine learning</h3><ul><li>scikit-learn: train/test split, regression, classification, metrics, overfitting.</li><li>Project 1: predict something real (house prices, exam scores, churn) with a clean notebook and README.</li></ul><h3>Weeks 7–9: generative AI</h3><ul><li>Call an LLM API, prompt templates, structured JSON output, embeddings.</li><li>Project 2: the RAG app (see “RAG From Scratch”), with an evaluation table.</li></ul><h3>Weeks 10–11: ship it</h3><ul><li>Wrap the project in an API (FastAPI or Spring Boot) and a simple web page.</li><li>Deploy on a free tier. Add logging, rate limits, and an <code>.env</code> file for keys (never commit keys).</li></ul><h3>Week 12: get hired</h3><ul><li>Portfolio: 2 strong projects beat 10 tutorials. Each needs a demo link, a 30-second video and a README with results.</li><li>Resume: one line per project with a metric (“answers 87% of 60 test questions correctly”).</li><li>Interview prep: explain your project end to end, trade-offs you made, and how you would scale it.</li><li>Apply to 10 roles a day: AI engineer intern, ML intern, GenAI developer, data analyst with AI.</li></ul><h3>Daily routine (1.5 hours)</h3><p>30 min learn → 45 min build → 15 min write notes or a LinkedIn post about what you built.</p>'
